<Doc
  title="Privacy Policy — Chatick"
  description="What Chatick stores, why, who else sees it, and how to get it deleted."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

  <p>
    This describes what Chatick stores, why it stores it, who else it is shared with, and how you get rid of it. It is
    written to match what the software actually does.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>Account</h3>
  <p>
    When you sign in with Google we receive and store your <strong>email address, name and profile picture</strong>. We
    also keep your interface language, and a phone number only if you enter one yourself. We never receive your Google
    password.
  </p>

  <h3>What you put in</h3>
  <p>
    Messages, tasks, comments, time entries, documents, notes, files and resources you create or upload. This is your
    working content — we store it so the service can show it back to you and to the people in your projects.
  </p>

  <h3>Technical</h3>
  <p>
    Standard server logs (IP address, browser, requested pages, timestamps) kept for security and debugging, and an
    authentication token in your browser's local storage so you stay signed in. Chatick does not use advertising
    cookies and does not run third-party analytics or trackers on the application.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else processes it</h2>
  <p>To run the service, data passes through a small number of providers:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Anthropic</strong> — message content and related project data are sent to the language model so the AI
      dispatcher can summarise, route and answer. This is the core AI feature.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> — sign-in only; they confirm who you are.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare R2</strong> — object storage for uploaded files and avatars.</li>
    <li><strong>An email provider</strong> — to deliver invitations, notifications and digests.</li>
    <li><strong>Hetzner</strong> — the servers in Germany where the database runs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your data, and we do not share it for advertising. Nobody outside these providers gets access,
    except where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Public links are public</h2>
  <p>
    Chatick lets you publish a file, document, note, resource or message as a public link that works without signing
    in. Anyone with the link can read it, and search engines may find it if the link is posted somewhere public. That
    is the point of the feature — but it is your decision each time, and you can revoke any link, after which it stops
    working immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it lives, and for how long</h2>
  <p>
    Data is stored on servers in Germany (EU). We keep your content for as long as your account exists. Deleted
    projects and companies are removed along with their files. Deleted documents and notes are recoverable for 7 days,
    then purged. Server logs are rotated regularly.
  </p>

  <h2>Backups</h2>
  <p>
    The database is backed up regularly so that a failure does not cost you your work. Backups are encrypted and kept
    on a retention window, which means a deleted item may persist in a backup for a short period after deletion before
    it ages out.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All traffic runs over HTTPS.</li>
    <li>Stored credentials in the "Resources" section are encrypted before they reach the database.</li>
    <li>Access inside a project is governed by roles, and every project holds its own scoped access token.</li>
    <li>Sensitive actions — deleting a project or a company — require explicit confirmation and notify every member.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No service can promise perfect security, and we will not pretend otherwise. If you find a vulnerability, please
    write to <a href="mailto:support@chatick.com">support@chatick.com</a> — reports are welcome and taken seriously.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Wherever you live, and specifically under GDPR if you are in the EU, you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask what we hold about you and get a copy;</li>
    <li>correct anything wrong — most of it you can edit yourself;</li>
    <li>delete your account and its content;</li>
    <li>object to processing, or ask us to restrict it;</li>
    <li>complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these, write to <a href="mailto:support@chatick.com">support@chatick.com</a>. We answer within
    30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Chatick is not intended for anyone under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes materially, the date above changes and the change is noted in the
    <a href="/changelog">changelog</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions, data requests, anything else: <a href="mailto:support@chatick.com">support@chatick.com</a>.
  </p>
</Doc>
